;; FH-CALL-001 — a declared view var holds a non-IFn descriptor value.
;;
;; The law has two halves, and the second is the one that earns the first:
;; a declared view is not callable, AND it is not a map. A map-shaped
;; descriptor would answer `(the-view props)` as a lookup — returning nil
;; and rendering nothing, silently. The predicates below are asserted
;; against a view declared with `v/defview`, on the JVM and in
;; ClojureScript, from this one fixture.
{:fh/id "FH-CALL-001"
 :fh/law
 "v/defview binds its var to a small non-IFn descriptor value; a direct call raises and can never silently succeed."

 ;; predicate -> expected answer for a declared view
 :predicates {:view? true
              :ifn?  false
              :fn?   false
              :map?  false
              :coll? false}

 ;; Invoking the descriptor as a function raises on both hosts. The host
 ;; refuses the call before any framework code runs, so the exception is
 ;; the host's own — what the law fixes is that the call cannot SUCCEED.
 :direct-call {:raises true}}
